<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE ANDROID 12+ SYSTEM SPLASH (admin 2026-08-13: "native app lage, capacitor nahi").

  From Android 12 the SYSTEM draws the first frame itself, before a single line of app code runs. It
  reads `windowSplashScreenBackground` from the launch theme — and this project never set it, so that
  frame fell back to the AppCompat.Light window background: WHITE.

  So the very first thing every user on a modern phone saw was a white sheet, then the app's own dark
  splash, then the dark UI. capacitor.config.ts already fought exactly this flash one layer down
  ("the single most obvious 'this is a web page loading' moment in the whole launch") — but that
  config governs the Capacitor splash, which the system splash comes BEFORE. It could never reach here.

  DELIBERATELY ONLY THE COLOUR. `postSplashScreenTheme` and `windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon` are not
  set: this file's own history records that a splash "optimisation" once left the app frozen on its
  launch screen, and those two change the hand-off and the icon pipeline. A background colour is read
  by the system before the app starts and has nothing to hang on — it cannot repeat that failure.

  In values-v31 rather than values/ because the attribute exists only from API 31; older devices keep
  today's launch untouched.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBarLaunch" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="android:background">@drawable/splash</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/nbaiSurfaceDark</item>
    </style>
</resources>
